    <DataNode elementId="Yeast-Manan-Fragment-IV" textLabel="S. cerevisiae mannan fragment with 6-phospho-α(1,2)-mannosyl side branch" type="Metabolite">
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="chawkins, SRI, caspi">The mannan found in the cell walls of |FRAME: TAX-4932| is composed of a linear chain of &amp;alpha;-(1,6)-D-mannan decorated by side chains and attached to |FRAME: ASN| residues of proteins by a linkage unit consisting of two &amp;beta;-(1,4)-&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetylglucosamine residues. The composition of the side chains varies, but largely consists of &amp;alpha;-(1,3)-mannosyl-&amp;alpha;-(1,2)-mannosyl-&amp;alpha;-(1,2)-mannosyl chains. The side chain can be shorter, and can be branched as well. The structure shown here shows a partially degraded mannan fragment with a 6-phospho-&amp;alpha;(1,2)-mannosyl side branch</Comment>
